<!-- PRACTICAL 1                                -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>Practical 1: Project Initiation, Requirement Analysis, Sitemap, Wireframe & GitHub Setup</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Initiate the semester-long StudentHub portal by identifying problem scope, user roles (Admin & Student), key modules, navigation flow, sitemap, wireframes, project folder structure, and GitHub repository.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Theoretical Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>What is a URL and its parts?</strong> Uniform Resource Locator. Parts: Scheme/Protocol (<code>http://</code> or <code>https://</code>), Host/Domain (<code>localhost</code> or <code>charusat.edu.in</code>), Port (<code>:80</code> or <code>:443</code>), Path (<code>/studenthub/login.php</code>), and Query String (<code>?role=student&timeout=1</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>How does an HTML file get processed in a web browser?</strong> The browser downloads the HTML byte stream, parses tokens, builds the DOM (Document Object Model) tree, processes CSS to build the CSSOM, combines them into a Render Tree, performs layout/reflow, and paints the pixels on the display screen.</li>
  <li><strong>How is navigation flow managed?</strong> Managed through a shared navigation header (navbar) linking all core views consistently with breadcrumbs and active state highlights.</li>
  <li><strong>How are GitHub commits maintained?</strong> Incremental commits after completing each practical task using Git branch workflows.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Project Folder Structure:</h3>
<div class="code-box">studenthub/
├── index.php                 # Home landing page
├── login.php / register.php  # Auth & signup modules
├── student_dashboard.php     # Student portal
├── admin_dashboard.php       # Admin monitoring
├── admin_students.php        # Student CRUD & CSV export
├── admin_events.php          # Event CRUD & poster uploads
├── ajax_crud.html            # Asynchronous Fetch CRUD
├── api_students.php          # JSON REST endpoint
├── audit_logs.php            # Security traceability
├── db.php                    # PDO & MySQLi connection
├── style.css                 # Responsive stylesheet
├── script.js                 # UI interactivity & theme
└── events.json / students.json # JSON datasets</div>

