<h2>Practical 2: Semantic HTML5 Pages with Accessibility-Ready Structure</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Develop static HTML5 skeletons for at least 10 StudentHub pages such as Home, About, Register, Login, Dashboard, Events, Profile, Contact, Admin, FAQ, and Feedback using semantic tags and accessibility-ready structure.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Are semantic tags used properly?</strong> Yes. <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> contains brand logo and navigation, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> encapsulates links, <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> contains unique page content, <code>&lt;section&gt;</code> groups related themes, <code>&lt;article&gt;</code> handles standalone cards, and <code>&lt;footer&gt;</code> holds copyright and university links.</li>
  <li><strong>Are accessibility tags implemented?</strong> Included <code>&lt;a href="#main" class="skip-link"&gt;Skip to main content&lt;/a&gt;</code>, ARIA attributes (<code>aria-label</code>, <code>aria-expanded</code>, <code>role="alert"</code>), and descriptive <code>alt</code> tags for images.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key Code Snippet (Semantic Navigation & Skip Link):</h3>
<div class="code-box">&lt;a href="#main" class="skip-link"&gt;Skip to main content&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;header class="navbar"&gt;
  &lt;div class="nav-container"&gt;
    &lt;a href="index.php" class="logo"&gt;Student&lt;span&gt;Hub&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation"&gt;
      &lt;a href="index.php"&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;a href="about.html"&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;a href="dynamic.html"&gt;Events&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;a href="faq.html"&gt;FAQ&lt;/a&gt;
      &lt;a href="login.php"&gt;Login&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/nav&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;</div>

