<h2>Practical 3: Responsive UI Design using CSS Grid, Flexbox & Media Queries</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Design responsive layouts for Home, About, Registration, Dashboard, and Events pages using CSS Grid and Flexbox with mobile-first responsiveness.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How does the layout adapt for mobile, tablet, and desktop screens?</strong> CSS Media Queries (<code>@media (max-width: 768px)</code>) switch navigation menus from inline flex to collapsible hamburger drawers and switch multi-column CSS Grid (<code>repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr))</code>) into stacked single columns on smaller mobile screens.</li>
  <li><strong>Why use Grid vs Flexbox?</strong> Flexbox is used for 1-dimensional alignment (navbar rows, button bars), while CSS Grid is used for 2-dimensional card grids (stats cards, course links).</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key CSS Code Snippet (style.css):</h3>
<div class="code-box">/* Responsive Statistics Grid */
.stats-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
  margin: 20px 0;
}
/* Mobile-First Navigation Breakpoint */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .nav-links { display: none; flex-direction: column; width: 100%; }
  .nav-links.open { display: flex; }
  .grid-dashboard { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}</div>

