<h2>Practical 4: JavaScript DOM Manipulation, Event Handling & UI Interactivity</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Add dynamic UI components such as collapsible FAQ, modal popups, notification banner, hamburger menu, and light/dark theme switcher using JavaScript and localStorage.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How are DOM elements selected and manipulated?</strong> Using modern methods: <code>document.getElementById()</code>, <code>document.querySelectorAll()</code>, <code>element.classList.toggle()</code>, and <code>element.addEventListener()</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Is localStorage used for persistence?</strong> Yes. User theme preference (<code>'dark'</code> or <code>'light'</code>) is stored in <code>localStorage.setItem("studenthub-theme", theme)</code> so the visual theme is preserved across sessions and page reloads.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key JavaScript Snippet (script.js):</h3>
<div class="code-box">function initTheme() {
  const btn = document.getElementById("themeToggle");
  const saved = localStorage.getItem("studenthub-theme");
  if (saved === "dark") document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "dark");
  
  btn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const isDark = document.documentElement.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark";
    if (isDark) {
      document.documentElement.removeAttribute("data-theme");
      localStorage.setItem("studenthub-theme", "light");
      btn.textContent = "🌙";
    } else {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", "dark");
      localStorage.setItem("studenthub-theme", "dark");
      btn.textContent = "☀️";
    }
  });
}</div>

<div class="screenshot-placeholder">[INSERT SCREENSHOT: Light / Dark Mode Toggle & Collapsible Accordion]</div>

