<h2>Practical 5: Registration Form with Frontend Validation & User-Friendly Error Handling</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Create a student registration form with HTML5 input types and JavaScript Regular Expression validation for name, email, mobile number, password, course, semester, and terms acceptance.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Which RegEx patterns are used?</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Email: <code>/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/</code></li>
      <li>10-Digit Mobile: <code>/^[0-9]{10}$/</code></li>
      <li>Password Strength: Checked dynamically for uppercase letters, digits, and special characters.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>How are UX errors displayed?</strong> Real-time inline feedback spans below each input field turn red when invalid, preventing submission until corrected.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key Code Snippet (register.php JS Validation):</h3>
<div class="code-box">passInput.addEventListener('input', function() {
  const val = passInput.value;
  let score = 0;
  if (val.length >= 8) score++;
  if (/[A-Z]/.test(val)) score++;
  if (/[0-9]/.test(val)) score++;
  if (/[^A-Za-z0-9]/.test(val)) score++;

  meterBar.style.width = (score * 25) + '%';
  meterBar.style.backgroundColor = score &lt;= 1 ? '#ef4444' : (score === 2 ? '#f59e0b' : '#10b981');
});</div>

