<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- PRACTICAL 10                               -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>Practical 10: Secure Login/Logout with Sessions, RBAC & Inactivity Timeout</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Develop secure login and logout using PHP sessions. Verify passwords with <code>password_verify()</code>, regenerate session IDs, restrict unauthorized dashboard access with RBAC, and implement a 15-minute inactivity session timeout.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Why call <code>session_regenerate_id(true)</code>?</strong> Prevents Session Fixation attacks by assigning a new session token upon authentication.</li>
  <li><strong>How is session timeout implemented?</strong> In <code>auth.php</code>, <code>time() - $_SESSION['last_activity'] &gt; 900</code> terminates the session and redirects to <code>login.php?timeout=1</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key PHP Snippet (login.php & auth.php):</h3>
<div class="code-box">if ($user && password_verify($password, $user["password"])) {
  session_regenerate_id(true);
  $_SESSION["user_id"] = $user["user_id"];
  $_SESSION["role"] = $user["role"];
  $_SESSION["last_activity"] = time();

  if ($user["role"] === "admin") {
    header("Location: admin_dashboard.php");
  } else {
    header("Location: student_dashboard.php");
  }
  exit;
}</div>

<div class="screenshot-placeholder">[INSERT SCREENSHOT: Successful Login & Inactivity Timeout Notice]</div>

<div class="page-break"></div>

