<!-- PRACTICAL 11                               -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>Practical 11: Student Management CRUD with Search, Filter & CSV Export</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Build a student management module enabling admins to add, view, edit, search, filter, and delete students with prepared statements and confirmation dialogs.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How are SQL statements protected?</strong> Parameterized queries (<code>UPDATE students SET name=? WHERE student_id=?</code>) eliminate SQL injection vulnerabilities.</li>
  <li><strong>How is CSV export handled?</strong> Emits CSV headers (<code>header("Content-Type: text/csv")</code>) and writes records with <code>fputcsv()</code> to <code>php://output</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key PHP Snippet (admin_students.php):</h3>
<div class="code-box">// Export to CSV Extension
if (isset($_GET["export"]) && $_GET["export"] === "csv") {
  header("Content-Type: text/csv");
  header("Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=students_export.csv");
  $out = fopen("php://output", "w");
  fputcsv($out, ["ID", "Name", "Email", "Mobile", "Department", "Semester"]);
  $stmt = $pdo-&gt;query("SELECT student_id, name, email, mobile, department, semester FROM students");
  while ($r = $stmt-&gt;fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC)) fputcsv($out, $r);
  fclose($out);
  exit;
}</div>

