<!-- PRACTICAL 12                               -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>Practical 12: Event Management CRUD with Poster Upload & File Validation</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Build event management allowing admins to create, edit, search, and delete events with validated event poster image uploads (MIME type check, file size &lt; 2MB, random unique filenames).</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How is file upload security enforced?</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>MIME type check using <code>finfo(FILEINFO_MIME_TYPE)</code>: allows only <code>image/jpeg</code>, <code>image/png</code>, <code>image/webp</code>.</li>
      <li>File size checked: <code>$file['size'] &lt;= 2 * 1024 * 1024</code> (maximum 2MB).</li>
      <li>Name sanitization: <code>bin2hex(random_bytes(16)) . '.' . $extension</code> prevents directory traversal.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key PHP Snippet (admin_events.php):</h3>
<div class="code-box">function posterUpload(array $f, string $dir, string $url): ?string {
  if (!isset($f['error']) || $f['error'] === UPLOAD_ERR_NO_FILE) return null;
  if ($f['size'] &gt; 2 * 1024 * 1024) throw new RuntimeException('Max 2MB allowed.');
  $mime = (new finfo(FILEINFO_MIME_TYPE))-&gt;file($f['tmp_name']);
  $types = ['image/jpeg'=&gt;'jpg', 'image/png'=&gt;'png', 'image/webp'=&gt;'webp'];
  if (!isset($types[$mime])) throw new RuntimeException('Invalid image format.');
  $name = bin2hex(random_bytes(16)) . '.' . $types[$mime];
  move_uploaded_file($f['tmp_name'], $dir . $name);
  return $url . $name;
}</div>

<div class="screenshot-placeholder">[INSERT SCREENSHOT: Event Poster Upload & Event Management Table]</div>

