<!-- PRACTICAL 13                               -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>Practical 13: PHP JSON API & AJAX/Fetch-Based CRUD without Page Reload</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Create PHP RESTful JSON API endpoints for students (<code>api_students.php</code>) and consume them using Fetch API in <code>ajax_crud.html</code> to perform list, search, add, update, and delete asynchronously with zero page reloads.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How do endpoints return JSON?</strong> <code>header("Content-Type: application/json")</code> and <code>echo json_encode($response)</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>How is search debounced?</strong> A 300ms <code>clearTimeout</code> prevents excessive HTTP requests while typing.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key Code Snippet (ajax_crud.html):</h3>
<div class="code-box">// Asynchronous Fetch API POST
const res = await fetch('api_students.php', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ name, email, mobile, department, semester })
});
const result = await res.json();
if (res.ok) {
  showToast(result.message);
  fetchStudents(); // Refresh table asynchronously
}</div>

