<h2>Practical 14: Admin Dashboard with Role-Based Access Control & Audit Logs</h2>
<p><strong>Problem Definition:</strong> Develop an admin dashboard displaying user statistics, student counts, and recent activities using SQL aggregation, role-based menus, and an audit trail viewer.</p>

<h3>1. Key Questions & Analysis:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How are statistics computed?</strong> Using SQL aggregation: <code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM students</code>, <code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM events</code>, <code>SELECT COUNT(*) FROM audit_logs</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>What gets logged in audit_logs?</strong> User ID, action (e.g. <code>user_login</code>, <code>student_create</code>, <code>event_deleted</code>), activity details, client IP address, and timestamp.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Key PHP Snippet (admin_dashboard.php):</h3>
<div class="code-box">$studentCount = (int)$pdo-&gt;query("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM students")-&gt;fetchColumn();
$eventCount = (int)$pdo-&gt;query("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM events")-&gt;fetchColumn();
$userCount = (int)$pdo-&gt;query("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users")-&gt;fetchColumn();
$logCount = (int)$pdo-&gt;query("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM audit_logs")-&gt;fetchColumn();</div>

