<h3>2. University Lab Viva Preparation (Questions & Answers):</h3>
<div class="viva-box">
  <p class="viva-q">Q1: What is the purpose of session_regenerate_id(true)?</p>
  <p><strong>Ans:</strong> It prevents Session Fixation attacks by destroying the old session ID and generating a new cryptographic session ID immediately after a user logs in.</p>
</div>
<div class="viva-box">
  <p class="viva-q">Q2: How does Fetch API differ from traditional XMLHttpRequest (XHR)?</p>
  <p><strong>Ans:</strong> Fetch API returns Promises, providing cleaner async/await syntax, better error handling, and avoiding callback hell.</p>
</div>
<div class="viva-box">
  <p class="viva-q">Q3: Why should passwords never be stored using md5()?</p>
  <p><strong>Ans:</strong> MD5 has known collision vulnerabilities and can be cracked in seconds via precomputed rainbow tables. <code>password_hash()</code> uses bcrypt with salt and computational work factors.</p>
</div>
<div class="viva-box">
  <p class="viva-q">Q4: What is the difference between client-side and server-side validation?</p>
  <p><strong>Ans:</strong> Client-side validation gives immediate feedback to users in the browser but can be easily bypassed. Server-side validation is mandatory for security before executing database queries.</p>
</div>

